CAMPUS FUTURES FORUM 2027
Where higher ed figures out what's next
26-28 May | Brindlecove Conference Centre
==============================================================

Hi Mara,

Quick reminder before the weekend gets away from you: early-bird
registration for Campus Futures Forum 2027 closes this Monday,
8 March, at 11:59 pm Pacific. After that the full-conference pass
goes up by $240.

  >> Register at the early-bird rate:
     https://campusfutures.example/register?rate=early&src=em0306

Early-bird pass includes all three days, the opening reception on
the harbour terrace, workshop access and session recordings.
Teams of three or more from the same institution save a further 10%.


--------------------------------------------------------------
CALL FOR LIGHTNING TALKS - STILL OPEN
--------------------------------------------------------------

Got a five-minute story? We're looking for short, honest lightning
talks from the people doing the work: the pilot that surprised you,
the data you wish you'd had sooner, the process you finally retired.
No sales pitches, no slides with more than 30 words.

Themes this year:

  * Student services that actually scale
  * Data, privacy and trust on campus
  * Shared platforms across institutions
  * Teaching and learning after the hype cycle

Submissions close Friday 19 March. Speakers get a complimentary
day pass.

  >> Submit a lightning talk: https://campusfutures.example/lightning


--------------------------------------------------------------
ALSO AT THE FORUM
--------------------------------------------------------------

  * Keynote: "The Registrar's Office Is a Product Team Now"
  * Hands-on workshops on service design and accessible course
    materials (limited seats - book with your pass)
  * The "Unconference Hour" on day two, back by popular demand
  * Room block at the Quayline Hotel at the conference rate
    until 23 April

See you at Brindlecove!

Beatriz Solano
Conference Organizer, Campus Futures Forum
beatriz@campusfutures.example

